T}:T{
Defines a timer relative to when the service manager was first started. For system timer units this is very similar to OnBootSec= as the system service manager is generally started very early at boot. Its primarily useful when configured in units running in the per\-user service manager, as the user service manager is generally started on first login only, not already during boot.
